{"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Returns a sequence of pairs ("},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"n"}]},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"x"}]},{"type":"text","text":"), where "},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"n"}]},{"type":"text","text":" represents a"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"consecutive integer starting at zero and "},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"x"}]},{"type":"text","text":" represents an element of"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"the sequence."}],"schemaVersion":{"minor":3,"major":0,"patch":0},"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/swift\/defaultindices\/enumerated()"]}],"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/com.apple.Swift\/documentation\/Swift\/DefaultIndices\/enumerated()","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/com.apple.Swift\/documentation\/Swift","doc:\/\/com.apple.Swift\/documentation\/Swift\/DefaultIndices"]]},"kind":"symbol","primaryContentSections":[{"declarations":[{"platforms":["macOS"],"tokens":[{"text":"func","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"enumerated","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"() -> ","kind":"text"},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"EnumeratedSequence","preciseIdentifier":"s:s18EnumeratedSequenceV","identifier":"doc:\/\/com.apple.Swift\/documentation\/Swift\/EnumeratedSequence"},{"text":"<","kind":"text"},{"text":"Self","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":">","kind":"text"}],"languages":["swift"]}],"kind":"declarations"},{"content":[{"type":"heading","text":"Return Value","anchor":"return-value","level":2},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"A sequence of pairs enumerating the sequence.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}],"kind":"content"},{"kind":"content","content":[{"type":"heading","text":"Discussion","anchor":"discussion","level":2},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"This example enumerates the characters of the string “Swift” and prints","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"each character along with its place in the string.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"syntax":"swift","code":["for (n, c) in \"Swift\".enumerated() {","    print(\"\\(n): '\\(c)'\")","}","\/\/ Prints \"0: 'S'\"","\/\/ Prints \"1: 'w'\"","\/\/ Prints \"2: 'i'\"","\/\/ Prints \"3: 'f'\"","\/\/ Prints \"4: 't'\""],"type":"codeListing"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"When you enumerate a collection, the integer part of each pair is a counter","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"for the enumeration, but is not necessarily the index of the paired value.","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"These counters can be used as indices only in instances of zero-based,","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"integer-indexed collections, such as ","type":"text"},{"code":"Array","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" and ","type":"text"},{"code":"ContiguousArray","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":". For","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"other collections the counters may be out of range or of the wrong type","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"to use as an index. To iterate over the elements of a collection with its","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"indices, use the ","type":"text"},{"code":"zip(_:_:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" function.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"This example iterates over the indices and elements of a set, building a","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"list consisting of indices of names with five or fewer letters.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"syntax":"swift","code":["let names: Set = [\"Sofia\", \"Camilla\", \"Martina\", \"Mateo\", \"Nicolás\"]","var shorterIndices: [Set<String>.Index] = []","for (i, name) in zip(names.indices, names) {","    if name.count <= 5 {","        shorterIndices.append(i)","    }","}"],"type":"codeListing"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Now that the ","type":"text"},{"code":"shorterIndices","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" array holds the indices of the shorter","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"names in the ","type":"text"},{"code":"names","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" set, you can use those indices to access elements in","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"the set.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"code":["for i in shorterIndices {","    print(names[i])","}","\/\/ Prints \"Sofia\"","\/\/ Prints \"Mateo\""],"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing"},{"name":"Complexity","type":"aside","style":"note","content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"O(1)","type":"text"}]}]}]}],"metadata":{"externalID":"s:STsE10enumerateds18EnumeratedSequenceVyxGyF::SYNTHESIZED::s:SI","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"func"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"enumerated"},{"kind":"text","text":"() -> "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:s18EnumeratedSequenceV","text":"EnumeratedSequence"},{"kind":"text","text":"<"},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Self"},{"kind":"text","text":">"}],"extendedModule":"Swift","modules":[{"name":"Standard Library"}],"title":"enumerated()","roleHeading":"Instance Method","role":"symbol","symbolKind":"method","platforms":[{"introducedAt":"8.0","unavailable":false,"beta":false,"deprecated":false,"name":"iOS"},{"introducedAt":"8.0","unavailable":false,"beta":false,"deprecated":false,"name":"iPadOS"},{"introducedAt":"13.0","unavailable":false,"beta":false,"deprecated":false,"name":"Mac Catalyst"},{"introducedAt":"10.10","unavailable":false,"beta":false,"deprecated":false,"name":"macOS"},{"introducedAt":"9.0","unavailable":false,"beta":false,"deprecated":false,"name":"tvOS"},{"introducedAt":"1.0","unavailable":false,"beta":false,"deprecated":false,"name":"visionOS"},{"introducedAt":"2.0","unavailable":false,"beta":false,"deprecated":false,"name":"watchOS"}]},"sections":[],"references":{"